        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive intelligence collection tasking package stood up to monitor and assess the evolving cooperative relationships among Russia, China, Iran, and North Korea, consistent with the threat landscape outlined in the 2025 Annual Threat Assessment. The package should cover all four adversaries both individually and as a collaborative bloc, with particular focus on asymmetric and conventional hard-power activities directed against U.S. interests and regional partners, efforts to establish alternative trade, finance, and security architectures that compete with Western-led systems, and any indicators that hostilities involving one adversary could draw in another. Collection should span SIGINT, OSINT, HUMINT, and GEOINT streams, with priority weighting toward indications and warning of escalatory behavior that remains below the threshold of direct armed conflict with the United States. Reporting cadence should be weekly summaries feeding into a monthly integrated assessment suitable for congressional consumers and senior policymakers. All products must be releasable at the unclassified level with a separate classified annex where sourcing requires it. The tasking should be coordinated through the National Intelligence Council workflow and aligned with existing National Intelligence Priorities Framework guidance. We need the initial collection plan drafted and routed for approval by end of next week, with first reporting cycle to begin no later than thirty days after approval.",
